---
description: PanelKit conventions. Read AGENTS.md before adding a panel screen.
alwaysApply: true
---

# PanelKit

Read `AGENTS.md` first (Day 0). If it is missing, run `php artisan panel:blueprint`.

PanelKit is Vue + Inertia, not Livewire Filament. Use PanelKit APIs only.

- Keep the `layout` callback in `resources/js/app.ts`. Do not set `layout: null` on panel pages.
- Add screens with `make:panel-resource` / `make:panel-page`, not a hand-rolled controller.
- Page-first CRUD: create / edit / view stay dedicated routes, not Livewire modals.
- Keep `SharePanelProps` on the web middleware group.
- Keep `PanelShell` in `resources/js/layouts/PanelLayout.vue`.
- Forbidden: inventing `Filament\…`, `Forms\Components\…`, `CreateAction`, `EditAction`, `Tables\Actions\…`.
- Keep status colour tokens in `resources/css/app.css` (`--success`, `--warning`, `--info` and `@theme` `--color-*`). Without them badge utilities never compile. Run `panel:update` if doctor reports them missing.
- Run `php artisan panel:doctor` before you call it done.

Claude Code: `php artisan panel:blueprint --file=CLAUDE.md`.
